  "_profile_help": "Each of 'left'/'right' has its own settings: deadzone (0-1, center gate for physical stick noise); anti_deadzone (0-1, output floor to defeat a game's built-in deadzone); curve (1.0 linear, >1.0 finer precision near center, <1.0 twitchier); axial_deadzone (optional 0-0.95, overrides cardinal/bowtie slope width -- when omitted on bowtie/sloped_axial/hybrid and deadzone < 0.05, auto-derives from anti_deadzone * 0.45 so cardinal pans stay steady); outer_circle_clamp (optional bool, clamps diagonal magnitude <= 1.0 on axial/sloped_axial; defaults to true on hybrid); deadzone_shape: 'radial', 'radial_unscaled', 'bowtie' (cardinal bowtie lock + smooth C0 transition into angle-preserving radial anti-deadzone), 'axial', 'axial_unscaled', 'sloped_axial' (bowtie per-axis deadzone with smooth Hermite dominance scaling), 'sloped_axial_unscaled', or 'hybrid' (radial center + curve followed by bowtie per-axis shaping). sloped_dominance_curve (0.0-2.0+, default 1.0): controls how smoothly anti_deadzone ramps in on the minor axis in sloped_axial/hybrid.",
  "rescan_interval": 1.0,
  "reload_interval": 1.0,
  "debug_sample_rate": 5,
  "max_output_hz": 250
}